1
00:00:01,235 --> 00:00:02,169
Who are you

2
00:00:02,236 --> 00:00:03,170
EPISODE 13

3
00:00:03,237 --> 00:00:04,438
to tell Yu-na to go?

4
00:00:08,442 --> 00:00:10,978
-Look, her guardian has arrived.
-Guardian?

5
00:00:12,012 --> 00:00:13,013
Guardian?

6
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:15,782
You bastard, you always run your mouth!

7
00:00:15,849 --> 00:00:16,917
Say that again!

8
00:00:16,984 --> 00:00:19,887
What? Guardian? Guardian?

9
00:00:20,554 --> 00:00:22,122
-Let go.
-Why is it so loud?

10
00:00:22,189 --> 00:00:23,924
I'm about to get mad too.

11
00:00:23,991 --> 00:00:25,726
-Do get mad!
-What are you doing?

12
00:00:25,792 --> 00:00:27,628
-Get mad and do what?
-Hey, stop!

13
00:00:27,694 --> 00:00:29,363
-Say it! Say it!
-Hey, you punks!

14
00:00:29,429 --> 00:00:30,797
I said get mad!

15
00:00:30,864 --> 00:00:34,668
What's wrong with you two?
Are you crazy? What's gotten into him?

16
00:00:34,735 --> 00:00:36,270
Hyeok, what's with you?

17
00:00:36,336 --> 00:00:39,072
You punks, seriously. Follow me out.

18
00:00:39,139 --> 00:00:42,376
Never a peaceful day with these guys.

19
00:00:42,442 --> 00:00:44,444
What's up? Why's he like that to you?

20
00:00:44,511 --> 00:00:47,447
It's nothing. Don't worry about it.

21
00:00:51,552 --> 00:00:53,253
Come on, hurry up.

22
00:00:53,921 --> 00:00:55,956
What on earth is up with you two?

23
00:00:56,023 --> 00:00:58,825
What had two friends
on the verge of a fistfight?

24
00:00:58,892 --> 00:01:01,562
Don't worry.
They say kids grow up fighting.

25
00:01:01,628 --> 00:01:03,497
How could I not worry…

26
00:01:04,565 --> 00:01:07,234
-Is it really nothing?
-Yes.

27
00:01:07,301 --> 00:01:09,269
Still, it feels really good

28
00:01:09,336 --> 00:01:11,171
because you worry about me.

29
00:01:11,705 --> 00:01:14,608
Anyway, you two make up soon.

30
00:01:14,675 --> 00:01:16,843
Friends don't act like that, okay?

31
00:01:17,811 --> 00:01:20,414
-We'll see.
-What do you mean, "We'll see"?

32
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:22,849
Gosh, seriously.

33
00:01:27,921 --> 00:01:29,256
Han-cheol.

34
00:01:29,957 --> 00:01:33,193
Snap out of it. What's wrong now?

35
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:35,696
Don't talk to me. I'm in agony.

36
00:01:37,164 --> 00:01:39,633
Anyway, why did you two fight?

37
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:42,002
Min-gi keeps defending only Yu-na,

38
00:01:42,069 --> 00:01:44,171
so I got jealous and picked a fight.

39
00:01:44,237 --> 00:01:47,107
Jealous? Do you like Min-gi? Please.

40
00:01:47,174 --> 00:01:48,108
What?

41
00:01:48,175 --> 00:01:51,178
-Hyeok, do you swing that way too?
-What are you saying?

42
00:01:51,244 --> 00:01:54,314
Huh? No, no. Never mind, never mind.

43
00:01:54,381 --> 00:01:57,084
Look, there's Su-yeon.

44
00:01:57,150 --> 00:01:58,852
Every Saturday, okay?

45
00:02:02,823 --> 00:02:04,925
Who's that woman next to her?

46
00:02:08,962 --> 00:02:10,364
Who is she?

47
00:02:11,465 --> 00:02:14,201
The woman who loves the woman I love.

48
00:02:52,806 --> 00:02:55,976
Gosh, drinking in the rain again?

49
00:02:56,043 --> 00:02:59,312
Why? Is there a law
against drinking in the rain?

50
00:02:59,379 --> 00:03:00,914
What the heck?

51
00:03:02,149 --> 00:03:03,583
Oh? Isn't that Mi-yeong?

52
00:03:04,885 --> 00:03:07,087
Hey, Mi-yeong! Heading to work?

53
00:03:07,154 --> 00:03:08,155
Yes, Man-gu.

54
00:03:08,221 --> 00:03:10,057
By the way, about I-ji…

55
00:03:10,123 --> 00:03:12,159
Can't you fire her from your shop?

56
00:03:12,225 --> 00:03:14,695
Always testing "new menus" or whatever,

57
00:03:14,761 --> 00:03:17,197
that brat turns the house into a wreck!

58
00:03:17,264 --> 00:03:19,232
Why be like that? She's working hard.

59
00:03:19,299 --> 00:03:21,001
Working hard, my ass.

60
00:03:21,068 --> 00:03:24,171
I bet she quits in a few months again.

61
00:03:24,237 --> 00:03:25,605
Am I right, Sang-deuk?

62
00:03:25,672 --> 00:03:27,774
Wait, where did that guy go?

63
00:03:27,841 --> 00:03:30,811
-Uh… Sang-deuk was here too?
-Yes.

64
00:03:30,877 --> 00:03:33,380
He was just drinking makgeolli here.

65
00:03:33,447 --> 00:03:36,616
He was snapping at me. Then he said…

66
00:03:37,851 --> 00:03:38,985
Huh?

67
00:03:41,688 --> 00:03:43,790
What is he, a ninja or something?

68
00:03:43,857 --> 00:03:45,092
He vanished so fast.

69
00:03:46,860 --> 00:03:49,162
No, this isn't right.

70
00:03:49,229 --> 00:03:52,899
No more running away.
I'll settle this like a real man.

71
00:03:59,039 --> 00:04:00,874
Hey, this is seriously amazing!

72
00:04:00,941 --> 00:04:02,642
Unbelievable!

73
00:04:04,010 --> 00:04:06,847
How did they grow this much in a day?

74
00:04:06,913 --> 00:04:09,015
This is really moving.

75
00:04:09,082 --> 00:04:12,385
I'm even more moved that we grew them.

76
00:04:12,452 --> 00:04:14,354
What do I do? They're so pretty.

77
00:04:15,021 --> 00:04:17,324
Wow, what is this?

78
00:04:21,294 --> 00:04:24,598
Wow, it's a snail! It's so cute.

79
00:04:24,664 --> 00:04:27,200
Oh! Hey, it's a snail.

80
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:29,069
I raised one at home before.

81
00:04:29,136 --> 00:04:30,637
Wow, we even have snails…

82
00:04:30,704 --> 00:04:32,806
We raised snails with our cabbages!

83
00:04:32,873 --> 00:04:34,007
Yes!

84
00:04:41,815 --> 00:04:43,216
Hello?

85
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:44,718
Return-to-Farm Consultant!

86
00:04:44,785 --> 00:04:45,919
Yes, yes.

87
00:04:45,986 --> 00:04:49,189
Thanks to you,
they're growing so fast and healthy.

88
00:04:49,256 --> 00:04:51,491
Yes, thank you so much. Yes.

89
00:04:51,558 --> 00:04:56,196
And we have so many super cute snails!

90
00:04:56,263 --> 00:04:59,099
Yes, come see! They're so, so cute.

91
00:04:59,166 --> 00:05:00,667
Yes, okay.

92
00:05:02,903 --> 00:05:05,539
Sir, we have snails in our field!

93
00:05:05,605 --> 00:05:07,274
-Hello, sir.
-Hello!

94
00:05:08,675 --> 00:05:10,277
What on earth happened here?

95
00:05:10,343 --> 00:05:12,746
The Return-to-Farm Consultant called.

96
00:05:12,813 --> 00:05:14,681
He said snails swarmed your field?

97
00:05:14,748 --> 00:05:16,683
Yes, they're so, so cute!

98
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:20,787
What, cute? You clueless idiots!

99
00:05:22,556 --> 00:05:24,891
Part Two of the Apocalypse has begun.

100
00:05:25,926 --> 00:05:28,662
Part Two of the Apocalypse?

101
00:05:30,130 --> 00:05:34,334
Look at this, you idiots.
Those "cute" snails of yours

102
00:05:34,401 --> 00:05:37,137
gnawed it all into this pathetic mess.

103
00:05:37,204 --> 00:05:40,574
Um, how much could such tiny,
cute little things possibly eat?

104
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:42,776
Fine, feel free to leave them alone.

105
00:05:42,843 --> 00:05:46,680
Then before long, your cabbages
will vanish without a trace,

106
00:05:46,746 --> 00:05:49,316
and in the field, way plumper
than the cabbages,

107
00:05:49,382 --> 00:05:52,018
swarms of snails will teem everywhere.

108
00:05:52,085 --> 00:05:53,687
As I always say,

109
00:05:53,753 --> 00:05:55,655
go sell snails instead of cabbage.

110
00:05:56,923 --> 00:05:58,158
So what should we do?

111
00:05:58,225 --> 00:06:00,260
Even pesticides won't work on them.

112
00:06:00,327 --> 00:06:02,562
You have to kill each one by hand.

113
00:06:02,629 --> 00:06:03,697
No, wait.

114
00:06:03,763 --> 00:06:05,999
Kill these tiny, cute little things?

115
00:06:06,066 --> 00:06:08,735
Or else your cabbages die, you punk!

116
00:06:08,802 --> 00:06:12,105
If they're that cute,
take them home and live with them.

117
00:06:12,172 --> 00:06:14,908
Why is it so hard to grow cabbages?

118
00:06:17,544 --> 00:06:19,446
So, what are you going to do?

119
00:06:24,417 --> 00:06:26,353
I am so sorry.

120
00:06:31,424 --> 00:06:33,660
Sir, do we really have to kill them?

121
00:06:59,719 --> 00:07:01,421
That's why I'm asking again!

122
00:07:02,188 --> 00:07:04,124
Are you and I really

123
00:07:04,190 --> 00:07:07,027
nothing more than close,
like brother and sister?

124
00:07:07,093 --> 00:07:10,463
No, I don't want us to just be
like brother and sister.

125
00:07:10,530 --> 00:07:12,365
-Really?
-Yes!

126
00:07:21,207 --> 00:07:23,476
Sang-deuk, what brings you by so early?

127
00:07:24,544 --> 00:07:27,113
Mi-yeong, I need to talk to you.

128
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:35,522
-What is it?
-Um…

129
00:07:36,122 --> 00:07:37,991
So, about what happened yesterday.

130
00:07:38,058 --> 00:07:39,693
I mean…

131
00:07:44,297 --> 00:07:46,132
You don't have to say it. I know.

132
00:07:46,199 --> 00:07:48,001
Just a drunken mistake. Forget it…

133
00:07:48,068 --> 00:07:49,402
No!

134
00:07:50,103 --> 00:07:51,972
It wasn't a mistake.

135
00:07:52,038 --> 00:07:54,274
I meant it. I really meant it.

136
00:07:55,241 --> 00:07:56,776
Mi-yeong.

137
00:07:56,843 --> 00:07:59,379
Let's start over.
I'll take care of you.

138
00:08:00,046 --> 00:08:01,548
Sang-deuk.

139
00:08:02,849 --> 00:08:04,985
No, even so, this isn't right.

140
00:08:05,051 --> 00:08:08,955
Why? Don't you like me? Is that it?

141
00:08:09,022 --> 00:08:13,159
It's not that, but we can't do this.

142
00:08:13,226 --> 00:08:15,328
I'm divorced, and I have a child.

143
00:08:15,395 --> 00:08:17,163
And what if your mom finds out?

144
00:08:17,230 --> 00:08:19,966
Don't worry about that. I'll handle it.

145
00:08:20,033 --> 00:08:21,835
You just have to trust me.

146
00:08:23,570 --> 00:08:26,773
I won't let go of this hand again.

147
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:29,976
No matter what happens,
nothing can stop our love now.

148
00:08:31,311 --> 00:08:32,679
Sang-deuk.

149
00:08:34,547 --> 00:08:36,049
Excuse me, coming through.

150
00:08:41,321 --> 00:08:43,089
I won't let go of this hand again.

151
00:08:45,325 --> 00:08:48,194
Gosh, we have this many apples left?

152
00:08:48,261 --> 00:08:49,629
Oh, dear.

153
00:08:52,165 --> 00:08:55,402
Even when I go to the market myself,
they just won't sell.

154
00:08:55,468 --> 00:08:57,337
It's because our Indi County apples

155
00:08:57,404 --> 00:09:01,775
-have no recognition, no recognition.
-get no promotion, no promotion.

156
00:09:02,509 --> 00:09:05,378
-Is there a good way to promote them?
-All right.

157
00:09:05,445 --> 00:09:08,548
I'll go to the township office today
and work out a plan.

158
00:09:08,615 --> 00:09:10,283
Have some noodles first.

159
00:09:10,350 --> 00:09:11,885
-You're here!
-Let's all eat.

160
00:09:11,951 --> 00:09:13,920
-Oh, my.
-Goodness.

161
00:09:13,987 --> 00:09:16,022
Thank you so much.

162
00:09:16,089 --> 00:09:18,425
-Here, Yun-hui.
-Thank you, Man-gu.

163
00:09:23,963 --> 00:09:25,665
You always make it so well.

164
00:09:26,266 --> 00:09:29,436
My, Madam Kim, your cooking…

165
00:09:29,502 --> 00:09:31,905
I must say, you are truly remarkable.

166
00:09:32,572 --> 00:09:34,507
These noodles are a work of art.

167
00:09:34,574 --> 00:09:36,276
Oh, you're too kind.

168
00:09:37,010 --> 00:09:38,978
Please, have as much as you like.

169
00:09:39,045 --> 00:09:40,113
What? What is this?

170
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:42,215
Mom, why the sudden nasal voice?

171
00:09:42,282 --> 00:09:43,950
When did I ever do that?

172
00:09:44,017 --> 00:09:46,019
-Oh, this boy…
-Nyah, nyah!

173
00:09:47,153 --> 00:09:48,788
Why am I acting like this?

174
00:09:48,855 --> 00:09:51,825
Whenever I hear Mr. Han's voice,
I just lose my senses.

175
00:09:51,891 --> 00:09:54,394
Mom, don't be too shocked. Just listen.

176
00:09:54,461 --> 00:09:57,230
I'm seeing Mi-yeong again.
We're getting married too.

177
00:09:57,297 --> 00:10:00,100
Yes, I know she wronged me terribly.

178
00:10:00,166 --> 00:10:01,668
I know she's a divorced mom.

179
00:10:01,734 --> 00:10:04,938
But you know how love is.
You don't weigh pros and cons.

180
00:10:05,004 --> 00:10:08,408
No matter what you say, Mom,
I'm starting over with Mi-yeong.

181
00:10:08,475 --> 00:10:11,611
Disown me or not, do whatever you want!

182
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:17,083
That's how I have to say it,
but this is really driving me crazy.

183
00:10:17,150 --> 00:10:19,786
No, I still have to tell her.

184
00:10:19,853 --> 00:10:21,521
Be brave, Sang-deuk.

185
00:10:26,459 --> 00:10:29,562
Where were you roaming all day
before crawling in now?

186
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:33,266
I had an errand to run.
Um, Mom, I have something to tell you.

187
00:10:33,333 --> 00:10:34,701
Hey, Sang-deuk.

188
00:10:34,767 --> 00:10:36,469
I took a nap earlier today.

189
00:10:36,536 --> 00:10:38,071
I had the most awful dream.

190
00:10:38,138 --> 00:10:39,405
-A dream?
-Yes.

191
00:10:39,472 --> 00:10:43,076
Hey, you said you were marrying
that bitch Mi-yeong!

192
00:10:43,143 --> 00:10:44,811
And… then?

193
00:10:44,878 --> 00:10:47,514
What do you mean, "And then"?
I was so appalled

194
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:49,682
that I beat you with a club,

195
00:10:49,749 --> 00:10:52,852
and you ended up half-paralyzed!

196
00:10:52,919 --> 00:10:55,288
That dream felt so real.

197
00:11:01,694 --> 00:11:03,496
You had something to say? What?

198
00:11:03,563 --> 00:11:05,498
Oh… no, it's nothing at all.

199
00:11:12,539 --> 00:11:16,609
Residents of Hadurok-ri, please gather
at the village hall immediately.

200
00:11:16,676 --> 00:11:18,144
Village Head Kang Yun-hui

201
00:11:18,211 --> 00:11:21,281
Right when I'm busy,
you boss me around, boss me around.

202
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:22,382
Quick, sit down.

203
00:11:22,448 --> 00:11:24,484
Just sit down, you bastard.

204
00:11:24,551 --> 00:11:25,752
Hurry, hurry!

205
00:11:25,818 --> 00:11:29,022
You've all been worried
about the apples lately, right?

206
00:11:30,056 --> 00:11:32,859
We finally have a solution.

207
00:11:32,926 --> 00:11:35,428
-What is it?
-Don't be shocked, just listen up.

208
00:11:36,062 --> 00:11:38,765
They say that next week,
coming to our Indi County

209
00:11:39,599 --> 00:11:43,236
is Paldo Gangsan Singing Contest!
Paldo Gangsan Singing Contest!

210
00:11:45,371 --> 00:11:48,575
What's Paldo Gangsan Singing Contest
got to do with apples?

211
00:11:48,641 --> 00:11:51,678
We can go on there
and promote our Indi County apples.

212
00:11:51,744 --> 00:11:54,514
And if we feed Kim Song-hae an apple…

213
00:11:54,581 --> 00:11:57,250
that'll really promote
our apples, right?

214
00:11:57,317 --> 00:11:59,619
Oh, you're right. That's a good idea.

215
00:11:59,686 --> 00:12:02,188
So for Paldo Gangsan Singing Contest,

216
00:12:02,255 --> 00:12:04,691
we need to pick
our village representative.

217
00:12:04,757 --> 00:12:07,393
If you think,
"I'm so confident in my singing,"

218
00:12:07,460 --> 00:12:09,262
please raise your hand.

219
00:12:11,097 --> 00:12:12,565
That's me!

220
00:12:13,233 --> 00:12:16,002
To fairly pick
our village representative,

221
00:12:16,069 --> 00:12:18,972
how about holding an audition?
What do you think?

222
00:12:19,038 --> 00:12:20,440
An audition?

223
00:12:24,611 --> 00:12:26,879
What are you doing here?

224
00:12:26,946 --> 00:12:28,414
I am just sitting here.

225
00:12:28,481 --> 00:12:31,918
Why do you look so down?
Is something wrong?

226
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:37,290
The truth is,
today is my mother's birthday,

227
00:12:37,957 --> 00:12:40,260
and I feel bad I can't even call her.

228
00:12:40,326 --> 00:12:42,895
You can just call her.

229
00:12:44,564 --> 00:12:47,166
The boss won't let me
make international calls.

230
00:12:47,233 --> 00:12:50,970
I'm scared to go to town to call
in case I get caught in a crackdown.

231
00:12:51,037 --> 00:12:53,873
How much could that even cost, anyway?

232
00:12:54,507 --> 00:12:56,209
Here, use this.

233
00:12:56,276 --> 00:12:57,910
No, it is okay.

234
00:12:57,977 --> 00:12:59,612
What do you mean, it's okay?

235
00:12:59,679 --> 00:13:01,914
You must call on your mom's birthday.

236
00:13:01,981 --> 00:13:03,249
It's okay, so use it.

237
00:13:03,316 --> 00:13:05,451
Use it all you want. All you want.

238
00:13:07,086 --> 00:13:08,955
Thank you.

239
00:13:17,563 --> 00:13:21,034
Hello? Mother?

240
00:13:22,001 --> 00:13:23,369
It's me, Hwa-ran.

241
00:13:24,370 --> 00:13:26,172
Have you been feeling well?

242
00:13:28,174 --> 00:13:29,809
Yes.

243
00:13:30,710 --> 00:13:32,578
I am doing well.

244
00:13:36,749 --> 00:13:38,251
I really am.

245
00:13:38,318 --> 00:13:40,420
Oh, the fridge broke down?

246
00:13:40,486 --> 00:13:41,788
You got it fixed?

247
00:13:41,854 --> 00:13:43,222
That's good, then.

248
00:13:44,257 --> 00:13:46,826
Is the bathroom water running well?

249
00:13:47,393 --> 00:13:48,494
A tile cracked?

250
00:13:48,561 --> 00:13:51,531
How on earth? Oh, just like that?

251
00:13:51,597 --> 00:13:53,633
How could it just crack like that?

252
00:13:53,700 --> 00:13:56,803
Why is she fussing over
even a cracked bathroom tile?

253
00:13:56,869 --> 00:13:58,838
On an international call, no less.

254
00:13:58,905 --> 00:14:00,873
No wonder they don't let her call.

255
00:14:01,541 --> 00:14:03,376
Did you call someone to fix it?

256
00:14:03,443 --> 00:14:06,212
You say it's cracked, then it's not?

257
00:14:08,481 --> 00:14:10,917
Mother? Mother?

258
00:14:11,884 --> 00:14:13,853
The battery's dead.

259
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:16,356
Um, Ki-jun, do you have a battery?

260
00:14:16,422 --> 00:14:18,057
No, I don't.

261
00:14:18,658 --> 00:14:20,193
This is unbelievable.

262
00:14:22,395 --> 00:14:23,930
I'm sorry.

263
00:14:24,597 --> 00:14:28,334
It's been over three years
since I saw my mother's face,

264
00:14:28,401 --> 00:14:30,503
so I missed her so much, I just…

265
00:14:30,570 --> 00:14:32,972
Three years?

266
00:14:39,479 --> 00:14:41,514
Wow!

267
00:14:42,181 --> 00:14:43,883
You made all this by yourself?

268
00:14:43,950 --> 00:14:45,918
I just cooked with what was at home.

269
00:14:45,985 --> 00:14:47,286
Eat before it gets cold.

270
00:14:47,353 --> 00:14:51,324
Wow! How long has it been
since we had a proper meal?

271
00:14:51,391 --> 00:14:55,695
It feels like almost 30 years for me.

272
00:14:56,362 --> 00:14:59,899
Gosh, I'm seriously getting choked up.

273
00:15:00,533 --> 00:15:02,402
Wow, awesome! This is so good.

274
00:15:02,468 --> 00:15:03,636
-Right, Min-ho?
-Yes.

275
00:15:03,703 --> 00:15:08,307
Um, Yu-na,
can't you just live here forever?

276
00:15:09,242 --> 00:15:11,978
Ki-jun and Han-cheol
will regret missing this.

277
00:15:12,044 --> 00:15:13,279
-Right?
-Totally.

278
00:15:14,714 --> 00:15:17,116
Brr, it's cold. So cold.

279
00:15:17,183 --> 00:15:18,518
That smell…

280
00:15:18,584 --> 00:15:22,188
Oh my, why is the mood here so good?

281
00:15:23,456 --> 00:15:24,590
What is all this?

282
00:15:24,657 --> 00:15:27,360
I just cooked with what was on hand.

283
00:15:27,427 --> 00:15:31,264
Oh, so you did the cooking, Yu-na.

284
00:15:32,031 --> 00:15:34,467
That's why the mood here was so good.

285
00:15:35,101 --> 00:15:36,702
Honey.

286
00:15:37,503 --> 00:15:39,972
-Is it delicious?
-Huh?

287
00:15:40,039 --> 00:15:42,475
No way, of course not.

288
00:15:42,542 --> 00:15:45,378
Maybe I'm just craving
the ramen you make, darling.

289
00:15:45,445 --> 00:15:50,016
There are lots of dishes here,
but none of them look appetizing.

290
00:15:50,082 --> 00:15:51,317
All right, I get it.

291
00:15:51,384 --> 00:15:53,853
How would you live without me, dear?

292
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:56,122
-Exactly.
-Honey, just wait a moment.

293
00:15:56,189 --> 00:15:57,824
I'll make delicious ramen.

294
00:15:57,890 --> 00:16:00,493
Honey, today I can just make do with…

295
00:16:02,728 --> 00:16:05,331
You truly live an exhausting life.

296
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:09,702
I heard Paldo Gangsan Singing Contest
is coming.

297
00:16:09,769 --> 00:16:11,804
-Paldo Gangsan Singing Contest?
-Yes.

298
00:16:11,871 --> 00:16:14,540
They're prepping
tomorrow's village rep prelims.

299
00:16:14,607 --> 00:16:16,275
The whole town is going crazy.

300
00:16:16,342 --> 00:16:17,343
-Prelims?
-Yes.

301
00:16:17,410 --> 00:16:20,613
We'll pick a town rep
for Paldo Gangsan Singing Contest.

302
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:23,449
-It's to promote our apples.
-Is that so?

303
00:16:24,217 --> 00:16:26,085
Aren't these guys singers?

304
00:16:26,152 --> 00:16:27,920
They can just enter!

305
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:29,355
Oh, Uncle.

306
00:16:29,422 --> 00:16:31,457
Don't you know they're not residents?

307
00:16:31,524 --> 00:16:33,493
Anyway, you guys have work tomorrow.

308
00:16:33,559 --> 00:16:35,595
Meet at the community center, got it?

309
00:16:35,661 --> 00:16:37,029
Us?

310
00:16:37,697 --> 00:16:38,664
Do what?

311
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:54,814
All right, starting right now,

312
00:16:54,881 --> 00:16:57,216
for Paldo Gangsan Singing Contest,

313
00:16:57,283 --> 00:17:01,521
we will now officially begin
our Hadurok-ri village preliminaries!

314
00:17:02,154 --> 00:17:04,223
And today's special accompaniment

315
00:17:04,290 --> 00:17:06,492
will be played by Excellent Souls!

316
00:17:06,559 --> 00:17:08,094
Round of applause!

317
00:17:11,564 --> 00:17:13,432
And for today's special judging,

318
00:17:13,499 --> 00:17:16,235
with no school, local,
or blood ties to you all,

319
00:17:16,302 --> 00:17:18,170
not a lick of it to be found,

320
00:17:18,237 --> 00:17:20,239
Mr. Han Ki-jun of Excellent Souls

321
00:17:20,306 --> 00:17:22,675
and Mr. Kang Hyeok will do the honors!

322
00:17:24,944 --> 00:17:26,812
So now, with our hearts racing,

323
00:17:26,879 --> 00:17:29,549
let us welcome our first contestant!

324
00:17:29,615 --> 00:17:32,552
Contestant number one, come on out!

325
00:18:03,883 --> 00:18:06,319
Why'd I get dinged? Why ding me?

326
00:18:08,487 --> 00:18:11,457
First, your emotion is so excessive

327
00:18:11,524 --> 00:18:14,961
that it has a serious tendency
to make viewers uncomfortable.

328
00:18:15,027 --> 00:18:18,197
And your facial expressions
and gestures are a bit much.

329
00:18:18,264 --> 00:18:20,266
It's a textbook amateur look, I'd say.

330
00:18:20,333 --> 00:18:22,468
Personally, I'd prefer it more natural

331
00:18:22,535 --> 00:18:25,705
and in your own style,
so that's a bit of a shame.

332
00:18:25,771 --> 00:18:28,040
My score is…
I can't score you very high.

333
00:18:28,107 --> 00:18:30,710
-Next.
-What's wrong with my singing?

334
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:32,111
What's wrong with it?

335
00:18:32,178 --> 00:18:34,080
You punks know nothing about music!

336
00:18:34,146 --> 00:18:36,482
I got 100 on the karaoke machine! 100!

337
00:18:36,549 --> 00:18:38,017
I can't accept this!

338
00:18:38,618 --> 00:18:40,353
I don't accept it. Forget it!

339
00:18:40,419 --> 00:18:42,455
-I got 100 at karaoke!
-Man-gu!

340
00:18:42,521 --> 00:18:44,957
Good luck to you all.
I can't do this, I quit!

341
00:18:45,024 --> 00:18:46,926
Now, for Contestant number two,

342
00:18:46,993 --> 00:18:48,995
let us swiftly bring them out!

343
00:18:49,061 --> 00:18:51,697
Contestant number two!

344
00:18:52,832 --> 00:18:53,866
Here we go!

345
00:18:53,933 --> 00:18:56,569
Green mountains…

346
00:19:02,108 --> 00:19:04,176
-Hmph.
-All right, next.

347
00:19:45,818 --> 00:19:46,919
Honey!

348
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:51,090
Honey, you did great. Honey, honey!

349
00:19:51,157 --> 00:19:52,591
Honey!

350
00:20:30,896 --> 00:20:33,299
Not a single one is worth salvaging.

351
00:20:33,365 --> 00:20:35,267
Yun-hui, please just give up now.

352
00:20:35,334 --> 00:20:38,237
This is no good.
We'll just embarrass the village more.

353
00:20:38,304 --> 00:20:40,773
Come on, I told you it's not over yet.

354
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:42,975
We still have one last contestant.

355
00:20:44,210 --> 00:20:47,747
-Jeez.
-Last contestant, please come on out!

356
00:20:52,451 --> 00:20:53,819
Whoa, hey!

357
00:20:54,987 --> 00:20:57,356
What's this? Are you auditioning too?

358
00:20:58,124 --> 00:20:59,892
Just stick to playing music.

359
00:20:59,959 --> 00:21:00,926
Hey, hold on.

360
00:21:00,993 --> 00:21:03,696
What'll you do if your dad finds out?

361
00:21:04,296 --> 00:21:08,067
My dad went into town,
so don't worry and start the music!

362
00:23:21,967 --> 00:23:25,537
Hey, considering how you look,
you actually sing really well.

363
00:23:27,406 --> 00:23:29,041
What's wrong with how I look?

364
00:23:29,808 --> 00:23:32,144
You're in no position to say that.

365
00:23:32,211 --> 00:23:35,281
All right, making the finals
is important, too.

366
00:23:35,347 --> 00:23:37,483
Promoting our apples is the real key.

367
00:23:37,549 --> 00:23:41,620
In other words, we definitely have to
land an interview with Kim Song-hae.

368
00:23:41,687 --> 00:23:43,255
How do we do that?

369
00:23:43,322 --> 00:23:46,625
I stayed up last night watching
Paldo Gangsan Singing Contest.

370
00:23:46,692 --> 00:23:49,028
After analyzing over 200 old episodes,

371
00:23:49,094 --> 00:23:53,132
I figured out the type of person
Kim Song-hae usually interviews.

372
00:23:53,198 --> 00:23:57,770
First off, Kim Song-hae likes
people who wear funny costumes.

373
00:23:59,071 --> 00:24:00,639
-Costumes?
-Yes.

374
00:24:00,706 --> 00:24:03,275
So I prepared something special.

375
00:24:03,342 --> 00:24:05,044
Hold on a second.

376
00:24:10,482 --> 00:24:11,583
Here you go.

377
00:24:12,718 --> 00:24:16,088
You seriously want me to sing in this?

378
00:24:16,155 --> 00:24:17,957
Oh, come on.

379
00:24:18,023 --> 00:24:19,992
Your singing isn't what's important.

380
00:24:20,059 --> 00:24:22,995
Promoting our apples is the real key.

381
00:24:23,062 --> 00:24:24,330
Quit whining and do it.

382
00:24:26,432 --> 00:24:29,134
-All right.
-Kim Song-hae likes something else.

383
00:24:29,201 --> 00:24:31,103
Something more upbeat than ballads.

384
00:24:31,170 --> 00:24:32,604
He likes dance music.

385
00:24:32,671 --> 00:24:35,274
Sang-eun, you can dance too, right?

386
00:24:35,808 --> 00:24:37,042
Of course I can!

387
00:24:38,877 --> 00:24:40,746
Oh, my goodness! You're so sexy!

388
00:24:40,813 --> 00:24:42,548
Well, I'll be! Look at you go!

389
00:24:43,282 --> 00:24:44,817
Goodness gracious!

390
00:24:44,883 --> 00:24:46,552
Sit down.

391
00:24:51,657 --> 00:24:55,394
By the way, once this airs on TV,
will people overseas watch it too?

392
00:24:56,061 --> 00:24:57,930
-Sure.
-Probably.

393
00:24:57,997 --> 00:24:59,631
Why do you ask?

394
00:24:59,698 --> 00:25:01,066
We're doing dance music.

395
00:25:01,133 --> 00:25:03,335
Wouldn't a backup dancer be better?

396
00:25:03,402 --> 00:25:06,705
It'd be nice to have one.
But is there anyone who can do it?

397
00:25:06,772 --> 00:25:09,341
We might find someone if we look.

398
00:25:09,408 --> 00:25:11,977
Okay, we can look into that later.

399
00:25:12,044 --> 00:25:15,347
For now, we'll practice
in the Branch school percussion room.

400
00:25:16,015 --> 00:25:17,983
We'll start real practice tomorrow.

401
00:25:18,050 --> 00:25:20,352
Brace yourself, got it?

402
00:25:20,419 --> 00:25:21,854
Okay.

403
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:24,623
Um… as a condition
for using the practice room,

404
00:25:24,690 --> 00:25:26,959
the teacher asked for a little favor.

405
00:25:27,026 --> 00:25:29,795
You guys will have to handle that.

406
00:25:29,862 --> 00:25:32,598
Why? What is it this time?

407
00:25:32,664 --> 00:25:34,066
SMALL RURAL CULTURE CLASS

408
00:25:34,133 --> 00:25:36,802
GUITAR LESSONS WITH EXCELLENT SOULS

409
00:25:38,337 --> 00:25:41,240
Hey, quiet down. Sit still. Shh, shh.

410
00:25:41,306 --> 00:25:43,542
All right, look at me.

411
00:25:44,176 --> 00:25:46,345
This is called C.

412
00:25:46,412 --> 00:25:49,782
The C chord. C, C, C, C, C, C.

413
00:25:49,848 --> 00:25:51,683
Why is that C?

414
00:25:52,551 --> 00:25:55,287
If I say it's C, it's C. Just play.

415
00:25:55,354 --> 00:25:58,057
People agreed on that from the start.

416
00:25:58,123 --> 00:26:00,492
How's that C different from vitamin C?

417
00:26:04,396 --> 00:26:06,298
Hey, come listen to this.

418
00:26:10,903 --> 00:26:14,673
-Mom!

419
00:26:18,343 --> 00:26:20,112
Ugh, jeez.

420
00:26:20,779 --> 00:26:24,416
How can a tiny patch of field
have so many rocks in it?

421
00:26:24,483 --> 00:26:28,687
Why is it so much work
just to eat some lettuce, for real?

422
00:26:32,357 --> 00:26:35,527
What? What are you doing here?

423
00:26:35,594 --> 00:26:38,197
It'll take forever
to clear rocks like that.

424
00:26:38,263 --> 00:26:41,166
Jeez. Who said I needed your help?

425
00:26:41,233 --> 00:26:43,335
I said I don't need it.

426
00:26:48,640 --> 00:26:51,076
Hey, you won't even say thanks?

427
00:26:51,743 --> 00:26:54,813
Darn it. Who asked you to help?

428
00:26:57,649 --> 00:26:59,852
Do you still hate me?

429
00:27:03,822 --> 00:27:06,258
You were better when you didn't talk.

430
00:27:06,325 --> 00:27:08,460
Is that even a question right now?

431
00:27:08,527 --> 00:27:10,295
Yes, I hate you to death.

432
00:27:10,362 --> 00:27:13,065
I'll hate you till I die, you bastard.

433
00:27:16,001 --> 00:27:17,970
Hey, get up.

434
00:27:21,006 --> 00:27:23,709
-Let's get a drink. Been a while.
-Forget it, man.

435
00:27:23,775 --> 00:27:25,677
Think I'll get over it so easily?

436
00:27:25,744 --> 00:27:27,813
Suit yourself, man.

437
00:27:32,217 --> 00:27:35,254
Hey! If the side dishes aren't good,

438
00:27:35,320 --> 00:27:37,089
you know I barely drink, right?

439
00:27:39,858 --> 00:27:41,026
HADUROK-RI SENIORS

440
00:27:41,093 --> 00:27:44,096
Hey, don't pour your own drink.
It's bad luck.

441
00:27:44,163 --> 00:27:45,797
Lift your glass.

442
00:27:55,374 --> 00:27:57,509
You offer to buy me a drink for once,

443
00:27:57,576 --> 00:28:00,445
and it's just rice wine
and measly scraps of kimchi?

444
00:28:00,512 --> 00:28:02,314
It'll do. What more do you want?

445
00:28:03,448 --> 00:28:05,284
Cut the crap, man.

446
00:28:08,554 --> 00:28:11,623
Hey, what's all that stuff over there?

447
00:28:17,429 --> 00:28:19,798
EXCELLENT SOULS

448
00:28:26,905 --> 00:28:28,574
Hey.

449
00:28:29,908 --> 00:28:32,978
-This is your guitar, right?
-Yes.

450
00:28:33,045 --> 00:28:34,780
Wow, jeez…

451
00:28:34,846 --> 00:28:38,183
You know how shocked I was too
when I first saw this?

452
00:28:38,250 --> 00:28:39,318
Man…

453
00:28:39,384 --> 00:28:42,354
But why does that kid have this?

454
00:28:42,988 --> 00:28:44,623
I don't know.

455
00:28:49,061 --> 00:28:52,364
Anyway, it's been a while.
Should we warm up our fingers?

456
00:28:52,431 --> 00:28:55,334
Have you lost your mind?
Out of nowhere, you bastard.

457
00:28:55,901 --> 00:28:59,404
Do you take me for a guy
with nothing better to do, sir?

458
00:29:14,319 --> 00:29:17,556
Hold on, where did I leave my wallet?

459
00:29:17,623 --> 00:29:19,825
Did I leave it at the village hall?

460
00:29:21,660 --> 00:29:23,662
What is that sound?

461
00:29:42,314 --> 00:29:43,315
You killed it.

462
00:29:43,382 --> 00:29:44,983
Wouldn't I be amazing on TV?

463
00:29:45,050 --> 00:29:46,918
Right, you can really sing too.

464
00:29:49,921 --> 00:29:51,690
Ma'am, what are you doing?

465
00:29:57,396 --> 00:29:59,598
Huh? Dad!

466
00:30:01,833 --> 00:30:03,769
Oh, Sang-eun.

467
00:30:06,672 --> 00:30:08,940
-Hello.

468
00:30:09,007 --> 00:30:10,075
What are you doing?

469
00:30:10,142 --> 00:30:12,778
Oh, I just ran into an old friend…

470
00:30:16,548 --> 00:30:18,083
Can you play guitar too?

471
00:30:18,150 --> 00:30:20,519
What? "Can you play guitar too?"

472
00:30:21,119 --> 00:30:22,187
Hey, you punk!

473
00:30:22,254 --> 00:30:24,323
This guy, man, back in the day, man,

474
00:30:24,389 --> 00:30:27,426
was named one of South Korea's
three greatest guitarists!

475
00:30:27,492 --> 00:30:30,762
That's how good he was, punk.
You don't know squat!

476
00:30:30,829 --> 00:30:31,697
Oh, really?

477
00:30:31,763 --> 00:30:35,867
Of course, punk. This guitar
you were playing is his. It's his!

478
00:30:36,902 --> 00:30:39,905
-This guitar is his?
-Wait, hold on. Then what?

479
00:30:39,971 --> 00:30:43,342
Is he the idol you saw in the woods
when you were a kid?

480
00:30:43,842 --> 00:30:45,310
-Wow.
-Jeez.

481
00:30:46,278 --> 00:30:48,080
But who are you, sir?

482
00:30:48,146 --> 00:30:49,748
What? Me?

483
00:30:49,815 --> 00:30:51,817
Yes, I don't think we've met before.

484
00:31:05,664 --> 00:31:06,865
A farmer, a farmer.

485
00:31:07,532 --> 00:31:09,434
I run a weekend farm here…

486
00:31:09,501 --> 00:31:11,269
Oh, we farm too.

487
00:31:11,336 --> 00:31:14,272
But what's with that apple?

488
00:31:14,339 --> 00:31:15,574
Huh?

489
00:31:16,241 --> 00:31:19,077
Oh! It's nothing.

490
00:31:29,388 --> 00:31:32,190
It was gloomy,
and now it's finally pouring.

491
00:31:32,257 --> 00:31:34,993
The weather here is seriously weird.

492
00:31:38,697 --> 00:31:40,265
Hwa-ran.

493
00:31:41,032 --> 00:31:42,601
What do you need?

494
00:31:43,335 --> 00:31:44,870
I… have something to say.

495
00:31:44,936 --> 00:31:47,005
Something to say? What is it about?

496
00:31:47,873 --> 00:31:51,276
Could you do that later?
It's so distracting I can't talk.

497
00:31:51,877 --> 00:31:54,246
My apologies. But what is this about?

498
00:31:54,312 --> 00:31:57,549
-Um, Hwa-ran, can you dance?
-Dance?

499
00:31:57,616 --> 00:32:00,118
National Singing Contest
comes in a few days.

500
00:32:00,185 --> 00:32:03,455
-Want to try being a backup dancer?
-I cannot dance.

501
00:32:03,522 --> 00:32:04,656
Anyone can dance.

502
00:32:04,723 --> 00:32:06,558
Just move like this to the music.

503
00:32:06,625 --> 00:32:07,926
No, thank you.

504
00:32:07,993 --> 00:32:10,829
You said you wanted
your mom to see your face.

505
00:32:10,896 --> 00:32:13,031
-Pardon?
-If you go on TV,

506
00:32:13,098 --> 00:32:15,434
your mom will get to see your face.

507
00:32:15,500 --> 00:32:18,303
I heard a lot of people
watch it in Yanbian too.

508
00:32:19,004 --> 00:32:20,672
Ki-jun.

509
00:32:21,206 --> 00:32:22,774
I just thought I'd tell you.

510
00:32:22,841 --> 00:32:24,342
Don't get the wrong idea.

511
00:32:25,811 --> 00:32:28,180
What are you doing in the rain?
Where to?

512
00:32:28,246 --> 00:32:30,816
I have to go
to Mrs. Kim's house by today

513
00:32:30,882 --> 00:32:32,384
to pick something up.

514
00:32:32,451 --> 00:32:35,720
Does it have to be today?
It's raining. Just do it next time.

515
00:32:35,787 --> 00:32:37,522
A promise is a promise.

516
00:32:50,202 --> 00:32:51,336
Thank you.

517
00:32:51,403 --> 00:32:53,004
Don't mention it.

518
00:32:55,440 --> 00:32:58,743
You drive this cultivator really well.

519
00:32:58,810 --> 00:33:00,479
This is easy.

520
00:33:00,545 --> 00:33:02,280
Would you like to try it?

521
00:33:02,347 --> 00:33:03,815
No, I'm good.

522
00:33:03,882 --> 00:33:05,917
I'll teach you.

523
00:33:06,485 --> 00:33:10,422
This goes right, and this goes left.

524
00:33:10,489 --> 00:33:12,958
-Hold the right one.
-I hold the right?

525
00:33:13,024 --> 00:33:14,559
Wow, this is easy!

526
00:33:14,626 --> 00:33:16,127
I did that, right?

527
00:33:16,194 --> 00:33:17,562
Chugga-chugga.

528
00:33:25,904 --> 00:33:27,405
Sang-deuk!

529
00:33:27,472 --> 00:33:29,174
Hey, Mi-yeong.

530
00:33:30,542 --> 00:33:32,978
So, how did it go?

531
00:33:33,645 --> 00:33:37,349
-Your mom is against it, isn't she?
-Huh? Um, well…

532
00:33:38,116 --> 00:33:39,784
You haven't told her yet.

533
00:33:39,851 --> 00:33:42,721
No, I told her.

534
00:33:42,787 --> 00:33:44,389
I just told Mom straight up…

535
00:33:44,456 --> 00:33:47,225
"I'm getting back with Mi-yeong,
just so you know."

536
00:33:47,292 --> 00:33:49,861
She couldn't say a word after that.

537
00:33:49,928 --> 00:33:50,795
Really?

538
00:33:50,862 --> 00:33:53,031
I told you to just trust me.

539
00:33:53,098 --> 00:33:54,266
Don't worry at all.

540
00:33:55,133 --> 00:33:56,434
Sang-deuk.

541
00:34:07,512 --> 00:34:10,015
Sang-deuk, what are you doing here?

542
00:34:10,081 --> 00:34:11,583
Weren't you with someone?

543
00:34:11,650 --> 00:34:12,517
Who?

544
00:34:12,584 --> 00:34:14,219
-Nobody was here.
-Really?

545
00:34:14,286 --> 00:34:17,188
I'm going to church,
so get yourself some food.

546
00:34:17,255 --> 00:34:18,557
Okay, got it.

547
00:34:18,623 --> 00:34:21,159
-Don't worry, go on ahead.
-Okay.

548
00:34:24,729 --> 00:34:25,997
Mi-yeong!

549
00:34:28,133 --> 00:34:29,968
-Are you hurt?
-Sang-deuk.

550
00:34:30,035 --> 00:34:31,202
Come on, get up.

551
00:34:32,637 --> 00:34:36,141
What was that?
What happened, Sang-deuk?

552
00:34:36,207 --> 00:34:38,710
Actually, I haven't told my mom yet.

553
00:34:38,777 --> 00:34:39,945
I'm really sorry.

554
00:34:40,011 --> 00:34:42,347
But I'll definitely tell her today.

555
00:34:43,348 --> 00:34:45,116
Oh, I see.

556
00:34:45,784 --> 00:34:48,720
It's okay, honey.
Take your time if you feel pressured.

557
00:34:48,787 --> 00:34:50,855
No, I'm not pressured at all.

558
00:34:50,922 --> 00:34:53,291
I just missed the timing, that's all.

559
00:34:53,358 --> 00:34:56,261
I'll definitely tell her today,
so don't worry.

560
00:34:56,328 --> 00:34:58,096
And as for us…

561
00:34:58,163 --> 00:35:01,833
let's go on a date openly tomorrow.
You trust me, right?

562
00:35:01,900 --> 00:35:04,803
Of course I trust you.

563
00:35:06,638 --> 00:35:08,707
Gosh.

564
00:35:12,744 --> 00:35:16,314
Right, I'll definitely tell her today
and get her blessing.

565
00:35:22,053 --> 00:35:24,856
Mom! I have something to tell you!

566
00:35:24,923 --> 00:35:26,191
Mom!

567
00:35:26,992 --> 00:35:29,828
Mom, you know, Mi-yeong and I…

568
00:35:30,795 --> 00:35:32,263
Mom.

569
00:35:33,031 --> 00:35:34,299
Mom.

570
00:35:34,366 --> 00:35:36,601
Grandpa, what happened here?

571
00:35:36,668 --> 00:35:39,104
She collapsed at church.

572
00:35:39,170 --> 00:35:42,941
-Collapsed? Why?
-She dozed off while praying.

573
00:35:43,008 --> 00:35:46,077
She had a bad dream or something.

574
00:35:46,578 --> 00:35:48,146
What dream?

575
00:35:48,213 --> 00:35:51,383
She said she dreamed you and Mi-yeong
got married?

576
00:35:51,449 --> 00:35:53,585
She got such a huge shock,

577
00:35:53,652 --> 00:35:56,254
they say she collapsed as she got up.

578
00:35:56,321 --> 00:35:59,791
You know your mom has a weak heart.

579
00:36:00,692 --> 00:36:03,561
They said to be extra careful.

580
00:36:04,329 --> 00:36:07,799
So you had something to tell your mom?

581
00:36:07,866 --> 00:36:08,867
What is it?

582
00:36:08,933 --> 00:36:11,770
What? No, it's nothing.

583
00:36:36,594 --> 00:36:38,563
Dad, why are you home so late?

584
00:36:39,731 --> 00:36:41,366
Did you drink a lot?

585
00:36:41,433 --> 00:36:45,070
I met up with a friend for once,

586
00:36:46,071 --> 00:36:47,572
and I drank a lot.

587
00:36:48,740 --> 00:36:50,408
What were you doing, though?

588
00:36:50,475 --> 00:36:53,712
What do you think? I was studying!

589
00:36:53,778 --> 00:36:55,613
-Studying.
-Studying?

590
00:36:57,649 --> 00:36:59,184
Studying.

591
00:37:02,320 --> 00:37:03,955
Gosh.

592
00:37:07,292 --> 00:37:08,693
Hey.

593
00:37:13,698 --> 00:37:16,835
What's this?

594
00:37:16,901 --> 00:37:20,672
You need an outfit to go on
Paldo Gangsan Singing Contest.

595
00:37:22,474 --> 00:37:24,142
Dad!

596
00:37:27,779 --> 00:37:29,414
From now on…

597
00:37:29,981 --> 00:37:33,518
live the way you want, okay?

598
00:37:33,585 --> 00:37:37,689
Don't live like a coward like I did.

599
00:37:41,693 --> 00:37:43,461
In return,

600
00:37:44,562 --> 00:37:48,032
you really have to succeed.

601
00:37:48,099 --> 00:37:50,301
Thanks, Dad!

602
00:37:51,236 --> 00:37:53,238
Dad!

603
00:38:09,621 --> 00:38:11,623
Hey, aren't you catching snails?

604
00:38:13,591 --> 00:38:15,994
I'm not in the mood to catch snails.

605
00:38:16,060 --> 00:38:19,764
Stop scarfing down that cabbage!
You're scarfing down what's for sale!

606
00:38:21,533 --> 00:38:23,802
Why? What's wrong this time?

607
00:38:26,237 --> 00:38:27,772
Um, you know…

608
00:38:28,840 --> 00:38:34,078
What if I fell in love with someone
who could never love me back?

609
00:38:34,145 --> 00:38:36,281
So what should I do then?

610
00:38:36,981 --> 00:38:40,185
-What are you talking about?
-Just listen, okay?

611
00:38:41,085 --> 00:38:44,055
No matter how hard I try,

612
00:38:44,122 --> 00:38:48,026
she can never, ever, ever love me!

613
00:38:48,092 --> 00:38:50,061
-Then what should I do?
-What else?

614
00:38:50,128 --> 00:38:53,164
Wish her happiness and let her go.

615
00:38:54,699 --> 00:38:57,669
I should, right? I should let her go?

616
00:38:59,270 --> 00:39:00,839
Quit scarfing down cabbage!

617
00:39:00,905 --> 00:39:04,809
What? With all this cabbage,
can't I even eat a single head?

618
00:39:26,764 --> 00:39:28,499
You're doing great!

619
00:39:41,246 --> 00:39:44,749
Wow, oh my gosh, you're so good!

620
00:39:44,816 --> 00:39:47,619
Sang-eun, you're a real
all-around entertainer!

621
00:39:48,486 --> 00:39:50,989
Amazed already?
This is the tip of the iceberg.

622
00:39:51,055 --> 00:39:52,423
Oh, really?

623
00:39:52,490 --> 00:39:53,725
You are so amazing.

624
00:39:53,791 --> 00:39:55,293
How do you dance so well?

625
00:39:55,360 --> 00:39:59,297
Actually, I used to do some b-boying.

626
00:40:01,666 --> 00:40:03,635
I can do headspins too. Care to see?

627
00:40:03,701 --> 00:40:05,904
Sure, sure! Let's see it, let's see!

628
00:40:11,109 --> 00:40:13,745
Here come the dance moves!

629
00:40:15,580 --> 00:40:18,683
Oh, my goodness!

630
00:40:18,750 --> 00:40:20,818
Oh dear, oh dear!

631
00:40:20,885 --> 00:40:24,589
My gosh, she's spinning endlessly!
Spinning endlessly!

632
00:40:24,656 --> 00:40:25,757
Sang-eun!

633
00:40:29,060 --> 00:40:31,262
Ouch!

634
00:40:33,197 --> 00:40:35,566
Oh my, what on earth happened here?

635
00:40:36,100 --> 00:40:37,835
As you can see,

636
00:40:37,902 --> 00:40:40,271
Sang-eun hurt her neck practicing.

637
00:40:40,338 --> 00:40:42,607
For the Paldo Gangsan Singing Contest,

638
00:40:42,674 --> 00:40:44,075
our town needs a new rep.

639
00:40:44,142 --> 00:40:46,044
Please recommend someone, okay?

640
00:40:46,844 --> 00:40:48,813
Well, since there's no choice, I'll…

641
00:40:48,880 --> 00:40:53,351
Ma'am, you're top-tier tone-deaf.
Don't even think about it.

642
00:40:53,418 --> 00:40:56,287
Right, Yun-hui, you sing really well!

643
00:40:57,622 --> 00:40:58,990
Me?

644
00:40:59,057 --> 00:41:01,159
Oh, goodness, no.

645
00:41:01,225 --> 00:41:03,928
I've heard her, and she sings so well.

646
00:41:03,995 --> 00:41:06,364
Goodness, what is he talking about?

647
00:41:06,431 --> 00:41:08,232
Don't mind him. Don't mind him.

648
00:41:08,299 --> 00:41:10,301
This is no time to play hard to get!

649
00:41:10,368 --> 00:41:11,903
You said to promote apples?

650
00:41:11,970 --> 00:41:12,904
Just try it.

651
00:41:12,971 --> 00:41:14,939
I'll wait and see how good you are.

652
00:41:15,006 --> 00:41:17,575
He sure talks a lot, that guy.

653
00:41:33,124 --> 00:41:37,695
Could you have forgotten me?

654
00:41:39,330 --> 00:41:43,901
Those burning eyes?

655
00:41:46,437 --> 00:41:49,674
Could you have forgotten

656
00:41:49,741 --> 00:41:51,576
What happened back then,

657
00:41:52,543 --> 00:41:56,981
Those beautiful memories?

658
00:42:01,853 --> 00:42:03,921
-Wow, she's good!
-My goodness!

659
00:42:05,690 --> 00:42:09,360
You're good! Yun-hui, you should enter.

660
00:42:09,427 --> 00:42:11,929
-I couldn't, Sang-deuk.
-Men won't do as well.

661
00:42:11,996 --> 00:42:15,366
A young woman can win over the judges
a lot more easily.

662
00:42:15,433 --> 00:42:17,835
Well? She has potential, doesn't she?

663
00:42:17,902 --> 00:42:19,871
Aside from her slightly shaky pitch,

664
00:42:19,937 --> 00:42:21,406
it's passable enough.

665
00:42:21,472 --> 00:42:24,475
-You can help her with that.
-Excuse me?

666
00:42:24,542 --> 00:42:27,612
Why should I? I'm busy.
I have to catch snails too.

667
00:42:31,182 --> 00:42:32,550
So you can't do it?

668
00:42:34,152 --> 00:42:37,622
My friend says you're in debt?

669
00:42:37,688 --> 00:42:38,923
What?

670
00:42:40,591 --> 00:42:43,194
Your friends don't seem to know.

671
00:42:47,265 --> 00:42:49,500
I will do it! I will teach her!

672
00:42:49,567 --> 00:42:51,969
I will train her thoroughly.

673
00:43:07,752 --> 00:43:09,821
Jeez, stop. Just stop.

674
00:43:09,887 --> 00:43:11,589
Seriously, are you in pain?

675
00:43:11,656 --> 00:43:13,391
How can you dance like that?

676
00:43:13,458 --> 00:43:16,160
You're stiff as a board.
Totally stiff as a board!

677
00:43:17,228 --> 00:43:19,630
It's not like I've ever danced before!

678
00:43:19,697 --> 00:43:21,632
This is driving me crazy.

679
00:43:21,699 --> 00:43:24,936
Setting the singing aside,
this dancing will never work.

680
00:43:25,002 --> 00:43:26,938
Entering is impossible. Impossible.

681
00:43:27,004 --> 00:43:30,741
How about we get coached by an expert?

682
00:43:32,276 --> 00:43:34,011
An expert?

683
00:43:36,147 --> 00:43:38,583
Yu-na, are you sure it's okay?

684
00:43:39,217 --> 00:43:40,985
Yes, it's fine.

685
00:43:41,052 --> 00:43:43,421
I owe you one. I should pay you back.

686
00:43:44,655 --> 00:43:47,158
Yun-hui, Hwa-ran, watch Yu-na closely.

687
00:43:47,225 --> 00:43:48,860
She'll only show you once.

688
00:43:48,926 --> 00:43:50,361
Here we go, Yu-na.

689
00:43:50,428 --> 00:43:52,230
Start!

690
00:44:01,005 --> 00:44:03,307
Gosh, wait, wait, wait!

691
00:44:03,374 --> 00:44:05,076
What? Why?

692
00:44:05,143 --> 00:44:07,879
You expect me to do that right now?

693
00:44:07,945 --> 00:44:10,481
Those insanely cringeworthy moves?

694
00:44:10,548 --> 00:44:12,717
Then what? You won't go to the finals?

695
00:44:12,783 --> 00:44:14,685
Aren't you promoting the apples?

696
00:44:14,752 --> 00:44:16,721
Well, I mean…

697
00:44:27,231 --> 00:44:30,535
We dig at night and paint by day.

698
00:44:30,601 --> 00:44:32,136
When do we ever sleep?

699
00:44:32,203 --> 00:44:34,605
If you can't take it, then go back.

700
00:44:34,672 --> 00:44:37,341
Did you think pocketing
five billion won was easy?

701
00:44:38,543 --> 00:44:40,211
Darn it, I'm out of paint.

702
00:44:40,278 --> 00:44:42,213
I'll go get some paint.

703
00:44:44,482 --> 00:44:48,619
We should just do a sloppy job,
dig it up, and get out of here.

704
00:44:53,124 --> 00:44:55,593
-Excuse me.
-Oh my, you startled me!

705
00:44:55,660 --> 00:44:57,061
What do you want?

706
00:44:57,128 --> 00:44:59,430
I came here to tell you something.

707
00:44:59,497 --> 00:45:01,666
What? To me?

708
00:45:01,732 --> 00:45:05,603
I have a few favors to ask you
regarding Su-yeon.

709
00:45:05,670 --> 00:45:07,205
Favors?

710
00:45:12,777 --> 00:45:14,478
Like what?

711
00:45:14,545 --> 00:45:18,583
First, Su-yeon loves sweet potatoes.

712
00:45:19,217 --> 00:45:23,321
So make sure she never runs out,
and please keep bringing them to her.

713
00:45:25,990 --> 00:45:27,658
Right here.

714
00:45:28,993 --> 00:45:31,963
No one has dug up
the sweet potatoes here yet.

715
00:45:32,029 --> 00:45:35,633
If you go there,
you'll be able to get sweet potatoes.

716
00:45:37,335 --> 00:45:38,669
Second.

717
00:45:39,670 --> 00:45:42,073
In winter,
when you can't get sweet potatoes,

718
00:45:44,008 --> 00:45:47,678
please at least buy her dried ones
so she can keep snacking on them.

719
00:45:49,213 --> 00:45:50,881
And one last thing.

720
00:45:52,950 --> 00:45:54,785
Su-yeon occasionally swears.

721
00:45:55,886 --> 00:45:57,822
Still, please don't be shocked.

722
00:45:58,356 --> 00:45:59,991
Always smile for her.

723
00:46:01,892 --> 00:46:04,061
Hold on, wait!

724
00:46:04,128 --> 00:46:06,731
What on earth are you talking about?

725
00:46:06,797 --> 00:46:10,801
Why would I have to dig up
sweet potatoes for Su-yeon?

726
00:46:10,868 --> 00:46:13,004
Can't you do that for the one you love?

727
00:46:13,070 --> 00:46:15,072
What? What did you say?

728
00:46:15,139 --> 00:46:16,440
Love?

729
00:46:16,507 --> 00:46:18,643
I know everything.

730
00:46:18,709 --> 00:46:20,111
You can drop the act.

731
00:46:21,145 --> 00:46:23,214
What exactly do you know?

732
00:46:23,281 --> 00:46:26,250
That you and Su-yeon
have that kind of relationship.

733
00:46:26,317 --> 00:46:28,753
That the two of you are in love.

734
00:46:28,819 --> 00:46:30,288
I know all about it.

735
00:46:30,354 --> 00:46:32,823
That kind of relationship?

736
00:46:32,890 --> 00:46:35,126
In love?

737
00:46:41,699 --> 00:46:43,167
Why are you laughing?

738
00:46:43,234 --> 00:46:45,336
I'm being so serious right now.

739
00:46:46,237 --> 00:46:48,606
What are you talking about right now?

740
00:46:49,674 --> 00:46:50,908
Su-yeon.

741
00:46:50,975 --> 00:46:53,411
Hey, what's with this guy?

742
00:46:53,477 --> 00:46:55,179
He's a total nutcase.

743
00:46:55,246 --> 00:46:58,949
He says you and I
have that kind of relationship.

744
00:46:59,950 --> 00:47:01,886
You do not need to hide it.

745
00:47:02,453 --> 00:47:06,624
Actually, I saw everything.
The two of you were kissing.

746
00:47:07,325 --> 00:47:08,859
Kissing?

747
00:47:08,926 --> 00:47:10,928
It was a few nights ago

748
00:47:11,962 --> 00:47:14,999
in that alley over there
near the village hall, darn it.

749
00:47:16,634 --> 00:47:19,203
Near the village hall?

750
00:47:20,071 --> 00:47:22,039
Honestly, that's not what it was.

751
00:47:22,106 --> 00:47:23,574
Her mask had a loose thread,

752
00:47:23,641 --> 00:47:25,576
so I bit it off for her.

753
00:47:26,510 --> 00:47:28,179
What? Um… really?

754
00:47:28,245 --> 00:47:31,449
Yes, it's true!
What on earth were you thinking?

755
00:47:32,616 --> 00:47:35,086
Su-yeon, thank you so much.

756
00:47:35,152 --> 00:47:36,787
Of course not, Su-yeon.

757
00:47:36,854 --> 00:47:39,690
Thank you so much for not loving women.

758
00:47:39,757 --> 00:47:41,225
What are you doing? Let go!

759
00:47:45,730 --> 00:47:47,531
Thank you.

760
00:48:03,381 --> 00:48:04,982
Honey, you're here early.

761
00:48:05,049 --> 00:48:07,485
I was too excited to sit still.

762
00:48:07,551 --> 00:48:09,120
By the way, what's that?

763
00:48:09,186 --> 00:48:11,655
It's our first date in so long.

764
00:48:11,722 --> 00:48:13,357
I showed off my cooking.

765
00:48:13,424 --> 00:48:15,760
You're such a cutie pie.

766
00:48:17,194 --> 00:48:18,529
Right, I forgot water.

767
00:48:18,596 --> 00:48:20,197
Wait here, I'll go grab some.

768
00:48:20,264 --> 00:48:23,267
Don't bother, it's raining though…

769
00:48:32,810 --> 00:48:35,045
Sang-deuk, what are you doing here?

770
00:48:35,112 --> 00:48:38,315
Um, I just had a quick errand,
and I'm heading back now.

771
00:48:38,382 --> 00:48:41,118
Is that so? Great, let's go together.

772
00:48:41,952 --> 00:48:43,888
Um, well, the thing is…

773
00:48:44,555 --> 00:48:46,290
Why? Waiting for someone?

774
00:48:46,357 --> 00:48:49,160
What? Who could I be waiting for?

775
00:48:49,226 --> 00:48:50,961
Then get moving. I'm busy.

776
00:48:51,028 --> 00:48:53,564
What? Um… okay.

777
00:49:03,407 --> 00:49:05,342
Let's start with the feet.

778
00:49:05,409 --> 00:49:07,445
Right foot, left foot.

779
00:49:07,511 --> 00:49:09,513
Right foot, left foot.

780
00:49:09,580 --> 00:49:12,383
One, two, three. Okay, now the hands.

781
00:49:12,450 --> 00:49:14,952
One, two, three, four.

782
00:49:15,019 --> 00:49:17,455
One, two, three, four.

783
00:49:17,521 --> 00:49:19,490
Now do both at the same time.

784
00:49:19,557 --> 00:49:20,758
Start!

785
00:49:20,825 --> 00:49:23,561
Right, left, right, left.

786
00:49:23,627 --> 00:49:24,929
One, two, three, four.

787
00:49:24,995 --> 00:49:26,931
Stop! Just stop, seriously!

788
00:49:26,997 --> 00:49:28,499
Is that really so hard?

789
00:49:28,566 --> 00:49:30,601
I tried it back there and did fine.

790
00:49:30,668 --> 00:49:32,736
Seriously, just look at Yu-na.

791
00:49:32,803 --> 00:49:34,805
Do it so it's cute and pretty.

792
00:49:34,872 --> 00:49:37,107
What can I do if I just can't do it?

793
00:49:38,476 --> 00:49:41,445
Forget it. Let's just give up on this.

794
00:49:41,512 --> 00:49:44,682
The way I see it,
your body isn't built for dancing.

795
00:49:44,748 --> 00:49:47,418
-Stop it.
-I'm sorry I'm so bad at this.

796
00:49:48,886 --> 00:49:50,187
Let's take a break.

797
00:49:50,254 --> 00:49:52,990
Wait, we don't have time for a break…

798
00:49:53,057 --> 00:49:55,926
Why be like that? She's trying hard.

799
00:49:55,993 --> 00:49:59,196
Her body just won't cooperate.
Stop comparing her to Yu-na!

800
00:49:59,263 --> 00:50:02,399
I only said she's bad because she is!

801
00:50:02,466 --> 00:50:05,236
-I'm pretty good at this too.
-I can do it too.

802
00:50:09,306 --> 00:50:10,941
That little jerk.

803
00:50:11,008 --> 00:50:14,478
Humiliating me in front of Yu-na.

804
00:50:37,368 --> 00:50:39,036
Yun-hui?

805
00:50:39,970 --> 00:50:41,639
Yun-hui!

806
00:50:42,206 --> 00:50:46,510
She's sulking over a few words?
Where is she?

807
00:51:14,672 --> 00:51:16,607
What are you doing here?

808
00:51:16,674 --> 00:51:19,143
Wow, you've still got it.

809
00:51:19,643 --> 00:51:22,513
It really brings back old memories.

810
00:51:22,580 --> 00:51:26,350
I once fell head over heels
watching you play the piano.

811
00:51:30,387 --> 00:51:33,624
We had so much fun in this classroom.

812
00:51:34,425 --> 00:51:37,428
Anyway, they could remodel this place.

813
00:51:37,494 --> 00:51:41,031
It's still so shabby.
Nothing's changed since the old days.

814
00:51:41,098 --> 00:51:45,002
It's nice to have at least one thing
that never changes.

815
00:51:45,669 --> 00:51:47,938
-That's true.
-Of course.

816
00:51:50,307 --> 00:51:52,743
Want to see what really never changes?

817
00:51:52,810 --> 00:51:54,178
What is it?

818
00:51:59,283 --> 00:52:02,386
YUN-HUI ♡ MIN-GI

819
00:52:05,589 --> 00:52:07,925
It's here! It's still here!

820
00:52:07,992 --> 00:52:10,561
I can't believe this is still here.

821
00:52:11,495 --> 00:52:13,197
Was this your doing too?

822
00:52:13,263 --> 00:52:15,165
-Of course.
-How childish.

823
00:52:15,232 --> 00:52:17,334
You think that's all? There's more.

824
00:52:17,401 --> 00:52:20,304
-Come over here.
-More?

825
00:52:22,806 --> 00:52:25,342
-Come here, come here.
-Honestly.

826
00:52:26,543 --> 00:52:27,578
Here it is!

827
00:52:27,645 --> 00:52:28,979
YUN-HUI ♡ MIN-GI

828
00:52:29,046 --> 00:52:31,315
Oh my goodness, it's here too.

829
00:52:31,382 --> 00:52:34,318
You wrote it so tiny.
You really squeezed it in there.

830
00:52:34,385 --> 00:52:36,787
Wow, when did I write this?

831
00:52:37,655 --> 00:52:39,156
What are you two doing here?

832
00:52:39,223 --> 00:52:40,524
Hey, Yu-na.

833
00:52:40,591 --> 00:52:43,527
What were you looking at so closely?

834
00:52:46,730 --> 00:52:50,167
-What's this?
-Uh, just graffiti I did as a kid.

835
00:52:50,834 --> 00:52:52,369
Oh, that's right.

836
00:52:52,436 --> 00:52:54,705
You said Yun-hui was your first love.

837
00:52:54,772 --> 00:52:59,209
Uh, I was young and immature then.

838
00:52:59,276 --> 00:53:02,446
Still, you were really cool back then.

839
00:53:03,414 --> 00:53:05,349
Let's get back to practice.

840
00:53:05,416 --> 00:53:08,118
I'm done for today. I'm tired.

841
00:53:08,185 --> 00:53:11,255
You have no persistence, none at all.

842
00:53:12,256 --> 00:53:14,024
It's okay if I go, right?

843
00:53:14,091 --> 00:53:16,827
Hey, I'll show you around the school.
Come here.

844
00:53:19,763 --> 00:53:23,600
This place is old and needs remodeling.

845
00:53:30,541 --> 00:53:33,110
YUN-HUI ♡ MIN-GI

846
00:53:40,350 --> 00:53:41,785
What are you doing?

847
00:53:42,519 --> 00:53:45,422
Uh, I wasn't doing anything.

848
00:53:45,489 --> 00:53:47,324
But what brings you here?

849
00:53:47,391 --> 00:53:51,361
I was worried about your practice,
so I came to check on you.

850
00:53:51,428 --> 00:53:55,165
But judging by your face,
it doesn't seem to be going well.

851
00:53:55,232 --> 00:53:56,934
No, I mean…

852
00:53:57,000 --> 00:54:00,938
Yu-na just dances so well,

853
00:54:01,004 --> 00:54:04,141
I got intimidated and couldn't dance.

854
00:54:07,144 --> 00:54:09,713
Then should I help you out?

855
00:54:10,514 --> 00:54:11,815
You?

856
00:54:12,583 --> 00:54:14,351
You even know how to dance?

857
00:54:14,418 --> 00:54:17,421
I used to be a huge hit at the clubs.

858
00:54:17,488 --> 00:54:19,757
In return, next time,

859
00:54:19,823 --> 00:54:21,759
how about granting me one wish?

860
00:54:21,825 --> 00:54:24,695
A wish? Jeez.

861
00:54:25,929 --> 00:54:27,264
All right, fine.

862
00:54:27,331 --> 00:54:30,234
But teach me to dance properly, okay?

863
00:54:37,841 --> 00:54:39,743
Who's…

864
00:54:39,810 --> 00:54:42,312
Sang-deuk, is that you?

865
00:54:43,447 --> 00:54:46,984
Wait, wait a second.

866
00:54:57,127 --> 00:55:00,564
Why do you always show up
at times like this?

867
00:55:00,631 --> 00:55:03,167
-Sorry.
-But you're just getting here?

868
00:55:04,201 --> 00:55:06,503
Um, I'm sorry about earlier.

869
00:55:06,570 --> 00:55:09,072
Sun-bun suddenly showed up…

870
00:55:09,139 --> 00:55:12,142
Actually, my mom collapsed yesterday.

871
00:55:12,209 --> 00:55:14,444
So I couldn't tell her yet. But…

872
00:55:14,511 --> 00:55:15,979
Um, listen.

873
00:55:16,847 --> 00:55:18,749
You know, maybe we…

874
00:55:20,117 --> 00:55:21,618
shouldn't try so hard.

875
00:55:21,685 --> 00:55:24,454
What? What do you mean by that?

876
00:55:24,521 --> 00:55:26,089
I said I'll tell her today.

877
00:55:26,156 --> 00:55:28,358
It's not because of you.

878
00:55:28,926 --> 00:55:30,828
Honestly, earlier,

879
00:55:30,894 --> 00:55:33,964
when I saw Sun-bun,
I instinctively hid too.

880
00:55:34,031 --> 00:55:35,299
Somehow, I was scared.

881
00:55:35,365 --> 00:55:39,870
Isn't that all because
we can't be proud of each other?

882
00:55:40,637 --> 00:55:42,673
-Mi-yeong.
-Sang-deuk.

883
00:55:43,340 --> 00:55:46,844
Let's rethink our relationship.

884
00:55:48,111 --> 00:55:50,013
I'll head inside first.

885
00:55:56,153 --> 00:55:59,356
Okay, push your hips back more.

886
00:55:59,423 --> 00:56:00,591
Right, hips back.

887
00:56:00,657 --> 00:56:03,961
And wave your arms cutely, cutely.

888
00:56:04,027 --> 00:56:06,897
-Cutely.
-Cutely, cutely.

889
00:56:06,964 --> 00:56:09,299
Cutely, cutely. Isn't it like this?

890
00:56:09,366 --> 00:56:11,835
-Now, push your hips back.
-Okay.

891
00:56:11,902 --> 00:56:13,804
Move your arms cutely, cutely.

892
00:56:13,871 --> 00:56:15,639
-Cutely, cutely.

893
00:56:15,706 --> 00:56:17,307
Cutely…

894
00:56:19,042 --> 00:56:20,477
What's wrong?

895
00:56:20,544 --> 00:56:23,914
It's just a little awkward.

896
00:56:27,417 --> 00:56:29,753
Did your heart just flutter for me?

897
00:56:29,820 --> 00:56:32,856
What? My heart fluttered? Oh, please.

898
00:56:32,923 --> 00:56:35,726
Now I've heard it all.
What a laughable load of crap.

899
00:56:52,142 --> 00:56:54,244
22 MISSED CALLS, 12 NEW MESSAGES

900
00:56:59,416 --> 00:57:01,285
MISSED CALLS

901
00:57:01,351 --> 00:57:03,387
PRETTY MIN-A

902
00:57:08,091 --> 00:57:12,029
Hello? Yu-na? Where are you right now?

903
00:57:12,863 --> 00:57:14,164
Hey.

904
00:57:14,231 --> 00:57:17,200
I'm out somewhere. Is everything okay?

905
00:57:17,267 --> 00:57:19,236
How could everything be okay?

906
00:57:19,303 --> 00:57:21,605
The company is in total chaos now.

907
00:57:21,672 --> 00:57:23,740
And the boss is desperate to find you.

908
00:57:24,408 --> 00:57:27,311
-Really?
-You're okay, right?

909
00:57:27,377 --> 00:57:29,579
Everything's really okay, right?

910
00:57:29,646 --> 00:57:31,315
Yes, I'm fine.

911
00:57:32,249 --> 00:57:34,751
I'm doing well, so don't worry.

912
00:57:35,452 --> 00:57:37,988
Don't tell the boss that I called.

913
00:57:38,588 --> 00:57:40,257
I'll call you again.

914
00:57:45,095 --> 00:57:46,463
What are you doing up?

915
00:57:50,367 --> 00:57:52,336
I came out for some fresh air.

916
00:57:53,337 --> 00:57:55,272
It's chilly. You'll catch a cold.

917
00:57:57,607 --> 00:57:59,276
Put this on.

918
00:58:00,143 --> 00:58:01,812
There you go.

919
00:58:05,349 --> 00:58:08,318
Your heart fluttered earlier, right?
Come on, tell me.

920
00:58:08,385 --> 00:58:10,253
I'm so sick and tired of this.

921
00:58:10,320 --> 00:58:13,357
Aren't you tired of it? Stop joking.

922
00:58:14,891 --> 00:58:17,694
I'm nowhere near tired of it yet.

923
00:58:17,761 --> 00:58:21,698
So, it seems like
you really liked Yun-hui back then.

924
00:58:22,866 --> 00:58:24,434
I was practically a stalker.

925
00:58:25,302 --> 00:58:28,271
I followed her around
like a puppy all the time.

926
00:58:30,574 --> 00:58:33,076
Do you still have feelings for her?

927
00:58:34,244 --> 00:58:36,113
It's not like that.

928
00:58:38,482 --> 00:58:42,586
But honestly, I do worry about her.

929
00:58:43,587 --> 00:58:45,956
Seeing someone I once liked

930
00:58:46,023 --> 00:58:48,658
living such a hard life like this

931
00:58:49,326 --> 00:58:51,661
makes me feel sorry for her,

932
00:58:52,229 --> 00:58:54,297
and makes me feel uneasy.

933
00:58:55,866 --> 00:58:58,301
I told her it wasn't like that.

934
00:58:59,503 --> 00:59:01,438
Would you call it pity?

935
00:59:02,005 --> 00:59:04,441
A kind of sympathy?

936
00:59:04,508 --> 00:59:06,576
Something like that?

937
00:59:06,643 --> 00:59:08,111
I don't think that's it.

938
00:59:08,178 --> 00:59:10,647
Come on, I told you it's not.

939
00:59:10,714 --> 00:59:13,917
I really have zero feelings for her.

940
00:59:14,484 --> 00:59:15,952
That's good, then.

941
00:59:17,254 --> 00:59:20,190
Wow, there are so many stars.

942
00:59:20,791 --> 00:59:23,193
-Right?
-Yes.
